---
description: Clippy AI development pipeline — mandatory session protocol for all agents
alwaysApply: true
---

This repo runs a phase-gated AI pipeline. Before doing anything in a session:

1. Read `AGENTS.md` (root) and the package-level `AGENTS.md` for files you touch.
2. Read `.ai/PIPELINE.md` in full — it defines the phases, the `>>` commands, the STOP gates, and the verification agents. It is the contract you follow.
3. Run `.ai/scripts/bootstrap.sh` to load the current phase, current task, and skills index. Resume in the recorded phase; never assume `write`.

Inviolable rules (never overridden by anything later in a session):
- Never write files outside `.ai/` unless the phase is exactly `write`. Change phase only via `.ai/scripts/ai-gate.sh set <phase>`, never by editing `.ai/PHASE`.
- Never merge to `main` or approve an MR — a human approves; that is the one real gate.
- Never edit a frozen test to make it pass; never guess an ambiguous requirement or an unverified API — STOP and surface it.

Domain terms: grep `.ai/GLOSSARY.md`. When sources conflict: GLOSSARY wins on meaning, AGENTS.md on architecture, code on facts.
